          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A natural
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            that makes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
            into a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo =
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A} = R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"} category of chain complexes
            of
            = succeed "-modules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
          #TheTensorProdComplex.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y \in Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
              write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X \otimes Y)_\bullet \in Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              whose component in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              (the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+products+of+modules"} tensor products of modules
              whose degrees adds to
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo +
                        %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (X \otimes Y)_n
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\bigoplus_{i + j = n}
                    X_i \otimes_R Y_j
            %p
              and whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              is given on elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y)
              of homogeneous degree by the following formula:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi X
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo +
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi deg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi Y
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial^{X \otimes Y} (x, y)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\big(\partial^X x, y\big)
                    \\,+\,
                    (-1)^{deg(x)} \big(x, \partial^Y y\big)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi Ch
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_{Ch}
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              considered as a chain complex concentrated in degree 0.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#as_a_total_complex_of_a_double_complex As a total complex of a double complex
          %p
            The tensor product of chain complexes is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+complex"} total complex
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complex"} double complex
            which is the objectwise tensor product:
          #DoubleComplexTensor.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y \in Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A})
              write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \otimes Y_\bullet \in Ch_\bullet(Ch_\bullet(\mathcal{A}))
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complex"} double complex
              whose component in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n_1, n_2)
              is given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_{n_1} \otimes Y_{n_2} \in \mathcal{A}
            %p
              whose horizontal differential is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi hor
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial^{hor} \coloneqq \partial^X \otimes id_Y
              and whose vertical differential is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi vert
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi X
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msup
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial^{vert} \coloneqq id_{X} \otimes \partial^Y
          #AsTotalComplex.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The tensor product of chain complexes, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheTensorProdComplex"}
              is isomorphic to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+complex"} total complex
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complex"} double complex
              of def.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DoubleComplexTensor"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Tot
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Tot_\bullet (X_\bullet \otimes Y_\bullet)
                    \\simeq
                    (X \otimes Y)_\bullet
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p By direct unwinding of the definitions.
          %h3#as_day_convolution As Day convolution
          %p
            The following section is copied form an answer by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Campbell"} Alexander Campbell
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/revisions/359316/6"} MathOverflow
          %p
            The tensor product of chain complexes is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            product. The important thing to note is that, to define a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+structure"} monoidal structure
            on the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
